---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';

const SECTIONS = [
  { id: 'what-is-vmware', title: 'What is VMware?' },
  { id: 'what-is-nutanix', title: 'What is Nutanix?' },
  { id: 'vmware-strengths', title: 'VMware Strengths' },
  { id: 'nutanix-strengths', title: 'Nutanix Strengths' },
  { id: 'comparison', title: 'Comparison Table' },
  { id: 'which-one', title: 'Which One Is Better?' },
];
---

<Layout title="VMware vs Nutanix — Cheatsheet" description="Compare VMware virtualization and Nutanix hyperconverged infrastructure: strengths, differences, and which one fits your data center.">
  <main>
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
      <a href="/cheatsheet" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm mb-8" style="color: var(--accent)">
        ← back to cheatsheets
      </a>

      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest px-3 py-1 rounded-full" style="background: var(--accent); color: #1a1a1a">Infrastructure</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight mb-2" style="color: var(--text)">VMware vs Nutanix</h1>
      <p class="text-sm mb-6" style="color: var(--text-muted)">Two Powerful Technologies, Two Different Approaches</p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-8 text-xs font-mono" style="color: var(--text-faint)">
        <span>7 min read</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>7 sections</span>
      </div>

      <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-10 text-xs font-mono">
        {SECTIONS.map(s => (
          <li>
            <a href={"#" + s.id} class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full border transition-colors" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">
              {s.title}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <div id="what-is-vmware" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#what-is-vmware" class="hover-underline">What is VMware?</a>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
          VMware focuses mainly on <strong style="color: var(--text)">virtualization</strong>. It provides technologies like ESXi, vCenter, vMotion, HA, DRS, and FT to virtualize and manage workloads efficiently inside a data center. For years, VMware has been the backbone of enterprise virtualization — stable, mature, and trusted by organizations worldwide.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm font-bold mt-3" style="color: var(--accent)">VMware = Strong virtualization platform</p>
      </div>

      <div id="what-is-nutanix" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#what-is-nutanix" class="hover-underline">What is Nutanix?</a>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
          Nutanix focuses on <strong style="color: var(--text)">hyperconverged infrastructure (HCI)</strong>. Instead of managing compute, storage, and virtualization separately, Nutanix combines everything into a single software-defined platform. Simple deployment, centralized management, easier scalability. Modern, fast, efficient.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm font-bold mt-3" style="color: var(--accent)">Nutanix = Complete infrastructure platform with built-in simplicity</p>
      </div>

      <div id="vmware-strengths" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#vmware-strengths" class="hover-underline">VMware Strengths</a>
        </h2>
        <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
          <li>✓ Industry-leading virtualization</li>
          <li>✓ Advanced enterprise features</li>
          <li>✓ Strong ecosystem and integrations</li>
          <li>✓ Mature and stable environment</li>
          <li>✓ Excellent workload flexibility</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div id="nutanix-strengths" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#nutanix-strengths" class="hover-underline">Nutanix Strengths</a>
        </h2>
        <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
          <li>✓ Simplified infrastructure management</li>
          <li>✓ Hyperconverged architecture</li>
          <li>✓ Easy scalability</li>
          <li>✓ Reduced operational complexity</li>
          <li>✓ Strong automation capabilities</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div id="comparison" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#comparison" class="hover-underline">Comparison Table</a>
        </h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr class="text-left font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider" style="color: var(--text-faint)">
                <th class="p-3 border font-bold" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Feature</th>
                <th class="p-3 border font-bold" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">VMware</th>
                <th class="p-3 border font-bold" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Nutanix</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Core Focus</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Virtualization</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Hyperconverged Infrastructure</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Management</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">vCenter</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Prism</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Complexity</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">More enterprise-level, strong</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Simpler management</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Scalability</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Moderate to Advanced</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Extremely easy</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Storage</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Separate SAN/NAS often required</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Built-in distributed storage</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Learning Curve</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Moderate</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Easier for many admins</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Best For</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Large enterprise virtualization</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Modern HCI and simplified operations</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="which-one" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#which-one" class="hover-underline">Which One Is Better?</a>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
          Honestly — it depends on business requirements.
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border-2" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <p class="font-bold mb-1" style="color: var(--text)">Choose VMware if…</p>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted)">Your organization already has a strong VMware ecosystem and traditional infrastructure setup. VMware remains incredibly powerful in these environments.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border-2" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <p class="font-bold mb-1" style="color: var(--text)">Choose Nutanix if…</p>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted)">You want simplified operations, faster scaling, and modern HCI architecture. Nutanix becomes very attractive for greenfield deployments.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 p-4 rounded-xl border-2 text-center" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
        <p class="text-xs font-mono" style="color: var(--text-faint)">
          At the end of the day, both technologies are shaping the future of modern data centers — just in different ways.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 text-center">
        <a href="/" class="inline-block px-6 py-3 font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm border-2 transition-all" style="background: var(--accent); color: #1a1a1a; border-color: #1a1a1a; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 #1a1a1a; border-radius: 9999px">
          ← all cheatsheets
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://talz.net" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Cheatsheets", "item": "https://talz.net/cheatsheet/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "VMware vs Nutanix Cheatsheet", "item": "https://talz.net/cheatsheet/vmware-vs-nutanix/" }
    ]
  })} />
</Layout>
